# FieldScholar repository separation

This repository contains the public FieldScholar marketing website.

The related FieldScholar application lives at `../fieldscholar`.

`../fieldscholar` is READ-ONLY context unless the user explicitly instructs otherwise.

## While working in fieldscholar-web

- Never modify `../fieldscholar`.
- Never delete, move, rename, format, build, or deploy `../fieldscholar`.
- Never change the application's Firebase Hosting configuration.
- Never deploy the existing FieldScholar application.
- Never run an unscoped Firebase deployment (`firebase deploy` without `--only`).
- Marketing deployments must target only the marketing Hosting target: `firebase deploy --only hosting:marketing`.
- `fieldscholar.app` belongs to the existing application.
- `about.fieldscholar.app` belongs to the public marketing website.

## Safe checks before any write or deploy

1. Confirm `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` is this repository (`fieldscholar-web`).
2. Confirm the Hosting target is `marketing` and that it does not point at the app Hosting site.
3. Never include files from `../fieldscholar` in this repository's commits.
